-### Verification of the fixes
+### 1. Raw/digest namespace collision (Bug, accepted)
+
+Right, and worth noting *why* I'd missed it: I had considered an attempt key
+shaped like `sha256:<hex>` and dismissed it as vanishingly unlikely. Likelihood
+was the wrong lens — ids are opaque (§1.3), so nothing forbids that shape, and
+the collision is **deterministic** rather than probabilistic. One condition fixes
+it: a key that already starts with the digest prefix is digested too, so the
+verbatim branch can never emit a `sha256:`-prefixed id and the two forms occupy
+disjoint namespaces. Short keys stay readable.
+
+### 2. Duplicate model slices double-count `by_model` (Bug, accepted)
+
+Reproduced first: two `m1` slices of 1M input tokens each priced the attempt at
+`$6.00` (correct) while `by_model["m1"]` read `$12.00`. The attempt total is right
+and only the per-model figure is wrong, which is the hardest kind of wrong number
+to notice.
+
+Fixed at both ends. Producers **merge** repeated labels
+(`cost_from_reported`) rather than rejecting the attempt — a bridge reporting one
+slice per gateway call legitimately names a model twice, the numbers are
+additive, and dropping the attempt would lose real spend. And `CostEntry` now
+**rejects** duplicate labels via a validator, because the wire accepts a
+`CostEntry` from any client and a producer-side convention is not an invariant.
+Post-fix: attempt `$6.00`, `by_model["m1"]` `$6.00`.
+
+### 3. Stale comment contradicting the floor-marker fix (Nit, accepted)
 
